// Warcraft 12x12 path constraint.
//
// Edges are supplied as a probabilistic relation `edge(u, v)` from the
// Python side: 264 ground tuples, indexed by row-major node ids
// (node_id = row * 12 + col, so source = 0, sink = 143).
//
// We treat edges as undirected (both directions reachable), derive
// transitive closure as `path/2`, then expose s-t reachability as the
// boolean predicate `valid_path(0)`.

rel undirected(x, y) = edge(x, y)
rel undirected(x, y) = edge(y, x)

rel path(x, y) = undirected(x, y)
rel path(x, z) = path(x, y), undirected(y, z)

rel valid_path(0) = path(0, 143)
